diff --git a/crates/apps/app/README.md b/crates/apps/app/README.md
index e22e1d6..5b05515 100644
--- a/crates/apps/app/README.md
+++ b/crates/apps/app/README.md
@@ -74,3 +74,52 @@ loading and hydration queueing now go through session-aware adapters:
 The old app-owned loader and queue implementation remain as internal migration
 seams until the real scene runtime is moved into `amigo-session` or
 domain-owned scene contributions.
+
+
+## Scene command dispatch migration status
+
+Hosted bootstrap now stabilizes through `stabilize_runtime_for_session`. Scene
+commands drained during startup orchestration are dispatched through
+`apply_scene_command_for_session` instead of the raw app-level dispatcher.
+
+The old `apply_scene_command(runtime, command)` function remains as a migration
+seam for tests and non-session callers until the dispatcher itself moves out of
+`amigo-app`.
+
+
+## Render session migration status
+
+`amigo-app` registers `RenderSessionService` in bootstrap alongside `SceneSessionService`
+so render lifecycle can be tracked as a session boundary.
+
+Current ownership remains app-side for actual extraction/composition/graph construction:
+
+- render extraction
+- composition building
+- frame graph building
+- submit/present call
+
+`RuntimeSession` now exposes render lifecycle entrypoints for future render adapters.
+
+## Scheduler migration status
+
+`amigo-app` still owns concrete system execution, but orchestration now uses
+`run_app_system_phase_for_session` when session is available so scheduler lifecycle is
+visible through `SchedulerSessionService`.
+
+Concrete system modules remain in app runtime until the next editor-friendly split.
+
+## Script command migration status
+
+`orchestration` and startup bridges now dispatch script commands through
+`dispatch_script_command_for_session` when `RuntimeSession` is available.
+
+Legacy `dispatch_script_command_with_runtime` remains as a non-session fallback path.
+
+## Dev console / debug boundary
+
+`amigo-app` hosts interactive runtime loop, input wiring, overlays, and startup UX.
+
+Engine-agnostic domain command ownership is currently planned via future domain plugins;
+dev-console registry/dispatcher currently acts as boundary seam while that split is
+implemented.
