diff --git a/crates/engine/session/README.md b/crates/engine/session/README.md
index 3bab037..5faa9fc 100644
--- a/crates/engine/session/README.md
+++ b/crates/engine/session/README.md
@@ -82,3 +82,75 @@ now:
 
 This keeps lifecycle ownership in `amigo-session` while later passes move the
 actual loader/handler implementation out of `amigo-app`.
+
+
+## Scene command dispatch boundary
+
+Etap 6 routes startup scene command dispatch through session-aware orchestration.
+
+The concrete dispatcher still delegates to app-owned `scene_runtime`, but hosted
+stabilization now uses `stabilize_runtime_for_session`, which sends scene commands
+through `apply_scene_command_for_session`. This keeps command lifecycle state
+visible through `SceneSessionService` while later passes move the real dispatcher
+out of `amigo-app`.
+
+## Scene clear lifecycle boundary
+
+Etap 7 records scene clearing as a first-class lifecycle phase.
+
+Runtime scene cleanup now marks `SceneSessionService` as `Clearing` before app-owned services are cleared, records `Empty` only after cleanup succeeds, and records an error if cleanup fails. A session-aware adapter exists for future call sites that already own `RuntimeSession`.
+
+## RenderSession boundary
+
+Etap 8 adds session ownership for render-frame lifecycle.
+
+`RenderSessionService` tracks render pipeline stages at session boundary:
+
+- frame extraction begin/end,
+- composition build,
+- graph build,
+- submit,
+- present,
+- last render error.
+
+`RuntimeSession` now exposes this boundary through:
+
+- `render_session_service()`
+- `begin_render_frame_extract()`
+- `complete_render_frame_extract()`
+- `complete_render_composition()`
+- `complete_render_graph_build()`
+- `complete_render_submit()`
+- `complete_render_present()`
+- `mark_render_error(...)`
+
+## SchedulerSession boundary
+
+Etap 10 exposes scheduler/system lifecycle through `SchedulerSession`.
+
+`SchedulerSessionService` records phase transitions and phase errors so per-frame
+system orchestration can be observed and controlled from the host boundary.
+
+`RuntimeSession` exposes these session boundaries through:
+
+- `scheduler_session_service()`
+- `begin_system_phase(...)`
+- `complete_system_phase(...)`
+- `mark_scheduler_error(...)`
+
+## ScriptSession boundary
+
+Etap 11 adds script command dispatch lifecycle ownership.
+
+`ScriptSessionService` records dispatch begin/complete/error for script commands so
+`orchestration` can produce deterministic diagnostics for command bridges.
+
+`RuntimeSession` now exposes:
+
+- `script_session_service()`
+- `begin_script_command_dispatch(...)`
+- `complete_script_command_dispatch()`
+- `mark_script_dispatch_error(...)`
+
+`dispatch_script_command_for_session` is the session-aware entrypoint expected by
+orchestration and host bridges.
